"""MCP ToolAnnotations for all SassyMCP tools (v1.16.0).

Curated by source-code analysis of the tool implementations in
sassymcp/modules/*. Each entry carries all four MCP annotation booleans
explicitly; do not rely on spec defaults.

ANNOTATION POLICY (uniform, implementation-verified)
---------------------------------------------------
* destructiveHint=True only when a tool deletes data, silently overwrites
  data the caller did NOT designate as the output, mutates system / device /
  registry state, or performs an irreversible or difficult-to-reverse action.
  Writing export files, screenshots, archives, or downloads the user
  explicitly requested is NOT destructive — even though those tools are also
  not read-only. (A desktop screenshot is pure observation plus a requested
  PNG write; it is not destructive. Duplicating a directory tree is likewise
  not destructive.)
* readOnlyHint=True only when the tool performs no state mutation at all.
  A tool that writes even a caller-requested file (export, screenshot,
  archive, download) is readOnlyHint=False.
* idempotentHint=False for anything that consumes state, appends, or has
  side effects that compound on repeat calls (e.g. sassy_session_read
  consumes buffers; sassy_move fails on a second identical call because the
  source no longer exists and destination-exists is refused).
* openWorldHint=True when the tool touches the network, external services,
  or devices beyond the local machine.
"""

